Stormbringer is from the Elric Saga books by Michael Moorcock.  I
specifically bought them because of the reference in nethack, and I
actually haven't been too impressed with them.  I've only read the first
of three volumes, and I've been meaning to ask if someone who's read
them all would say they get better and are worth reading the other two
volumes.  So far it's been much too melodramatic for my taste, and
really hasn't been *A* saga so much as a number of almost completely
unrelated wanna-be-but-are-much-too-short-and-undeveloped-to-be-sagas.
Heck, Schlock Mercenary has more of a saga feel to me than the Elric
books, and funny beats melodramatic emo any day, IMO (I loved that N
Habits list, dogscoff).

As for making Stormy more vocal, hearing "the moaning of tormented
souls" would be more in-line with the source mythos than an "ominous
hum", but it definitely could be more vocal, and an "ominous hum" would
be a good laugh, although I dunno how well I'd like cross-mythoi
references in a single object.


